<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica mohair prices steady at second winter sale.</title>
<headline>SAfrica mohair prices steady at second winter sale.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Good demand for South African mohair continued at the second sale of the winter selling season but prices were generally unchanged, the Mohair Board said on Wednesday. 95 percent was sold.</p>
<p>Approximate prices in South African cents a kg:</p>
<p>Adults	  long	 2600-2770	(2600-2654)</p>
<p>		  medium     1890-2650	(2450-2610)</p>
<p>		  short	2452-2522	(2432-2520)</p>
<p>Young Goats   long	 2510-3500	(2630-2880)</p>
<p>		  medium     2470-2650	(2480-2572)</p>
<p>		  short	2470-2530	(2450-2500)</p>
<p>Fine Kids     long	 3200-5092	(3500-5702)</p>
<p>		  medium     3000-5010	(3052-3700)</p>
<p>		  short	2800-3562	(3210-3652)</p>
<p>The third winter sale of the season is scheduled for October 1, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
